## Why This Is Asked
This tests ability to design governance for cross-team experimentation, balancing speed with reliability and data integrity.

## Key Concepts
- KPI ownership and charter
- Preflight power analysis and data-quality gates
- Guardrails: latency, error rate, quotas
- Feature flags, canary and cohort rollouts
- Artifacts: experiment charter, data map, rollback plan

## Code Example
```javascript
function shouldRollout(experiment, metrics) {
  const {power, mde, dataQuality} = metrics;
  if (!experiment.flagsEnabled) return false;
  if (power < experiment.requiredPower) return false;
  if (!dataQuality.ok) return false;
  if (metrics.latency > experiment.maxLatency) return false;
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would thresholds vary by product area?
- How would you measure guardrail impact on velocity and reliability?

## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses your ability to align cost, risk, and velocity in a multi-team, multi-region environment with shared data platform infrastructure.

## Key Concepts
- FinOps and cost governance in cloud-native environments
- SLOs/SLIs and error budget policies
- Multi-tenancy isolation and privacy controls
- Budgeting, chargeback, and ownership models
- Incident costing and blameless postmortems
- Experiments to validate operational readiness

## Code Example
```javascript
// Tagging for cost ownership
function tagResource(resource, owner, project) {
  return {
    ...resource,
    tags: {
      owner: owner,
      project: project,
      costCenter: getCostCenter(owner),
      environment: process.env.ENV
    }
  };
}
```
